{"id": "clm:02b1346f73324b1da74e6984f446e05e872174bbd709a652dc615046a74194d0", "type": "statement", "text": "The independent mongodb-atlas-admin 0.0.1 Rust wrapper README marks Rolling Index and Create One Rolling Index unchecked. Its endpoint inventory therefore does not establish an implemented client operation. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.rs/crate/mongodb-atlas-admin/latest/source/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Administration API rolling index endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:a8fa90f272de4c928a47ff3c7b82686a2a790c4e416a0bc2ff370fcb03ababda", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:858a12fe7f7c5a40e57ef867188dfc5061ae4627ac38e7078932439d4782760e", "ev:beb914829a4b733d5961ac97d272de06b2a58cec90569792bb4bb730a9187128"]}
{"id": "clm:79740d3f841d4eb87674e909c46d9c48077147089ff2358e1330405cebe44168", "type": "statement", "text": "A June 8, 2020 Stack Overflow question reports production index-build performance problems and asks whether rolling-build automation is available. A June 9 user comment by D. SM says Atlas apparently offers automated rolling index builds and links MongoDB documentation; this thread does not document an API endpoint implementation or diagnose the reported performance issue. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/62272251/mongodb-rolling-index-build", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Administration API rolling index endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:a8fa90f272de4c928a47ff3c7b82686a2a790c4e416a0bc2ff370fcb03ababda", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7ec608bcb914c86423789ce1cefbcaec8a713c067cc3e0c7ba85c40d1408c4d0"]}
